\begin_layout Standard
We can now further simplify this by using the fluctuation dissipation theorem.
 First, let's calculate the derivative 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\left(-\frac{\partial n_{B}}{\partial\nu}\right) & =\frac{\partial}{\partial\nu}\frac{1}{1-e^{\beta\nu}}\\
 & =\frac{-\beta e^{\beta\nu}}{\left(1-e^{\beta\nu}\right)^{2}}\\
 & =\beta n_{b}\left(\nu\right)\left(1+n_{b}\left(\nu\right)\right)
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
